    "codeAssessment": [
      "The v3 provenance successor is additive metadata: it pins the unchanged v2 candidate and exact two target pre/postimage hashes, current resolver/CLI/tests, adapter/adoption planner, and implementation receipt. It explicitly leaves old freeze and old producer-pin currentness unclaimed.",
      "The apply adapter accepts only the expected reviewed plan fingerprint, snapshots fixed source inputs, rebuilds the plan, and refuses if plan or blocker state changes.",
      "The public quality CAS accepts only plan and targets, uses fixed native filesystem operations, acquires an exclusive owner lock, re-reads current fixed authority and source bytes under that lock before preparation, and enforces exact ordered target/pre/postimage bindings.",
      "No effect path is available on this current cut: the live adoption plan has no root source-owner decision or exact two-target apply authorization.",
      "The shared owner lock serializes this governed CAS writer. The final pre-rename hash/mode read detects changes observed before rename; it is not a kernel-level compare-and-swap against an uncooperating external writer racing after that read, as documented in the writer.",
      "This new peer record is additive and is not consumed by the current adoption planner, whose fixed quality-peer ref remains the existing independent-peer.v2.json. No adapter or authority-reader source was changed; an owner-controlled successor workflow must decide whether and how to bind this record."
    ],
